          "modify_from": "The world xy location of the demonstrated block at the END of the demonstration, stored as [x,y]. Identify the block actually lifted, then track its physical identity continuously through all subsequent exchanges of positions; do not retain its original slot. At the video cycle write its final location. During execution retain this location unless the same block is visibly released at a displaced location, in which case update to its new resting xy. This identifies the rightmost red block in episode 70, the leftmost green block in 76 and 56, the leftmost red block in 6, and the demonstrated foreground red block in 95. Infer coordinates using calibration and the block's tabletop geometry, not image left/right as world axes. e.g. [0.014, 0.160]",
