          "modify_to": "At the video cycle identify the block that the hand lifts. Follow that physical block through the remaining video, including every exchange with an indistinguishable block, and write the fixed front-camera pixel coordinates [u,v] of its final resting top-face center. Do not attempt a world-coordinate conversion in the video cycle. Never select simply the slot originally grasped: exchanges can change which slot contains the target. During execution retain this value while the target is held or obscured; do not update for apparent image motion caused by lifting. When the same target is visibly resting after release at a displaced location, update to its top-face center in the front image. If that center is obscured at release, retain the previous value until a later current view reveals the same resting target's center, then update. Never update from another block. e.g. [127,103]"
