    },
    {
      "modify_from": "If completed_repetitions equals N and the released target is on the table with the open hand raised clear, move above the circular stop button at z=0.15, roll=-pi, pitch=0, yaw=0, keeping the gripper open. Localize the button's center, not the center of a neighboring cube.",
      "modify_to": "If completed_repetitions equals N and the released target is on the table with the open hand raised clear, move to button_location at z=0.15, roll=-pi, pitch=0, yaw=0, keeping the gripper open. Populate button_location from the first clearly visible calibrated execution view as specified in the memory instruction, using the circular top's center at approximately world z=0.02 m, not the tabletop plane, base, or a neighboring cube. Use the same stored xy for approaching, closing above, pressing, and retracting, even when the arm occludes the button. The localization surface height is distinct from the commanded pressing height."
    }
  ],
  "refused": ""
}
